#: ../../../cmake-modules/F2PY.rst:2
msgid "F2PY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:3
msgid ""
"The purpose of the F2PY –Fortran to Python interface generator– project is "
"to provide a connection between Python and Fortran languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:6
msgid ""
"F2PY is a Python package (with a command line tool f2py and a module f2py2e) "
"that facilitates creating/building Python C/API extension modules that make "
"it possible to call Fortran 77/90/95 external subroutines and Fortran 90/95 "
"module subroutines as well as C functions; to access Fortran 77 COMMON "
"blocks and Fortran 90/95 module data, including allocatable arrays from "
"Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:11
msgid "For more information on the F2PY project, see http://www.f2py.com/."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:13
msgid "The following variables are defined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:17
msgid "F2PY_EXECUTABLE      - absolute path to the F2PY executable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:21
msgid ""
"F2PY_VERSION_STRING  - the version of F2PY found\n"
"F2PY_VERSION_MAJOR   - the F2PY major version\n"
"F2PY_VERSION_MINOR   - the F2PY minor version\n"
"F2PY_VERSION_PATCH   - the F2PY patch version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:29
msgid ""
"By default, the module finds the F2PY program associated with the installed "
"NumPy package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:32
#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:41
msgid "Example usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:34
msgid ""
"Assuming that a package named ``method`` is declared in ``setup.py`` and "
"that the corresponding directory containing ``__init__.py`` also exists, the "
"following CMake code can be added to ``method/CMakeLists.txt`` to ensure the "
"C sources associated with ``cylinder_methods.f90`` are generated and the "
"corresponding module is compiled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:39
msgid ""
"find_package(F2PY REQUIRED)\n"
"\n"
"set(f2py_module_name \"_cylinder_methods\")\n"
"set(fortran_src_file \"${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/cylinder_methods.f90\")\n"
"\n"
"set(generated_module_file ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/"
"${f2py_module_name}${PYTHON_EXTENSION_MODULE_SUFFIX})\n"
"\n"
"add_custom_target(${f2py_module_name} ALL\n"
"  DEPENDS ${generated_module_file}\n"
"  )\n"
"\n"
"add_custom_command(\n"
"  OUTPUT ${generated_module_file}\n"
"  COMMAND ${F2PY_EXECUTABLE}\n"
"    -m ${f2py_module_name}\n"
"    -c\n"
"    ${fortran_src_file}\n"
"  WORKING_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}\n"
"  )\n"
"\n"
"install(FILES ${generated_module_file} DESTINATION methods)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindF2PY.cmake:65
msgid ""
"Using ``f2py`` with ``-c`` argument means that f2py is also responsible to "
"build the module. In that case, CMake is not used to find the compiler and "
"configure the associated build system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:3
msgid "The following functions are defined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:7
msgid ""
"Create a custom rule to generate the source code for a Python extension "
"module using f2py."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:10
msgid "add_f2py_target(<Name> [<F2PYInput>]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:11
msgid "[OUTPUT_VAR <OutputVar>])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:13
msgid ""
"``<Name>`` is the name of the new target, and ``<F2PYInput>`` is the path to "
"a pyf source file.  Note that, despite the name, no new targets are created "
"by this function.  Instead, see ``OUTPUT_VAR`` for retrieving the path to "
"the generated source for subsequent targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:18
msgid ""
"If only ``<Name>`` is provided, and it ends in the \".pyf\" extension, then "
"it is assumed to be the ``<F2PYInput>``.  The name of the input without the "
"extension is used as the target name.  If only ``<Name>`` is provided, and "
"it does not end in the \".pyf\" extension, then the ``<F2PYInput>`` is "
"assumed to be ``<Name>.pyf``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:25
msgid "Options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:27
msgid "``OUTPUT_VAR <OutputVar>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:28
msgid ""
"Set the variable ``<OutputVar>`` in the parent scope to the path to the "
"generated source file.  By default, ``<Name>`` is used as the output "
"variable name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:32
msgid "``DEPENDS [source [source2...]]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:33
msgid "Sources that must be generated before the F2PY command is run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:35
msgid "Defined variables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:37
msgid "``<OutputVar>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:38
msgid "The path of the generated source file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UseF2PY.cmake:43
msgid ""
"find_package(F2PY)\n"
"\n"
"# Note: In this case, either one of these arguments may be omitted; their\n"
"# value would have been inferred from that of the other.\n"
"add_f2py_target(f2py_code f2py_code.pyf)\n"
"\n"
"add_library(f2py_code MODULE ${f2py_code})\n"
"target_link_libraries(f2py_code ...)"
msgstr ""
